---
/* Component — PageHeader
 * The page's top bar. daisyUI's own .navbar-start/.navbar-center/.navbar-end
 * sub-parts are rented as-is for the wordmark / centre-content / controls
 * layout — their flex-basis-50%-plus-shrink mechanics already centre a middle
 * child correctly, so there is nothing to override there.
 *
 * The outer element keeps daisyUI's .navbar class, and this component's own
 * rule overrides it: display/align-items are redeclared explicitly (matching
 * daisyUI's values) so the box model here is fully self-contained rather than
 * leaning on daisyUI's layered rule, and min-height: 0 resets daisyUI's fixed
 * 4rem so block padding sizes the bar to its content.
 *
 * A full-width edge-to-edge band: as a direct child of Page (outside PageBody's
 * inline inset) it spans the whole window width on its own — no margins, no
 * bleed tricks — and the raised fill bleeds edge to edge with it. Flat and
 * cornerless, to read as chrome rather than a floating card. The inline padding
 * uses the same centred-column formula as PageBody: since padding insets the
 * *content* without shrinking the element's own box, the fill still spans full
 * width while the start/center/end content caps at --bravoixr-page-max and
 * lines up with the page column below. The fill themes with the page via the
 * semantic dark override. */
---

<header class="navbar">
  <div class="navbar-start"><slot name="start" /></div>
  <div class="navbar-center"><slot name="center" /></div>
  <div class="navbar-end"><slot name="end" /></div>
</header>

<style>
  .navbar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--bravoixr-spacing-5);
    min-height: 0;
    padding-block: var(--bravoixr-spacing-5);
    padding-inline: max(var(--bravoixr-spacing-10), calc((100% - var(--bravoixr-page-max)) / 2));
    background: var(--bravoixr-color-surface-raised);
  }
</style>
